# Three groups, one purpose each, in this order on purpose: git applies the LAST
# matching pattern, so the publication allowlist has to sit below the denials it
# inverts. Moving a group changes what a fresh clone contains.


# ---- 1. Build residue -------------------------------------------------------
# Written by a build, a test run, a package step or the OS. Never authored here.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info
build/
dist/
# A wheel built outside dist/ needs its own rule: an unignored stray wheel joins any
# tree mirrored with `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`, which a
# fresh clone never holds.
*.whl
node_modules
tags

# macOS junk (also stripped by: apex.sh clean)
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
__MACOSX
.fseventsd


# ---- 2. Local developer files -----------------------------------------------
# This working copy only. None of it is part of the app, and none of it ships.

# Agent and bench tooling working directories. The owner's scanners live under
# .claude/ by decision, so this one line already covers them.
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.trae/
.frappectl/
.frappectl.toml
skills-lock.json
# Symlink to the bench control tool, which lives outside this checkout.
ctl
.ctl/
.ctl.toml

# A nested checkout — worktree or vendored clone — is never this repo's content.
**/.git/

# Local-only rich demo generator: Arabic sample data, bench-only, never published.
apex/demo/

# Dead code archive.
archive/

# Local-only scratch scripts and reports.
scratch/
*.command
*.applescript
flash_actions_report.json

# Raw HTTP/curl response dumps — may capture live auth tokens.
curl_output*.txt
**/curl_output*.txt
*.curl

# Environment, secrets, and local runtime files.
.env
.env.*
*.local
*.secret
*secret*
*.key
*.pem

# Editor swap files.
*.swp


# ---- 3. Publication allowlist -----------------------------------------------
# Documents and data files are denied by TYPE first and re-included one named path
# at a time, so a new file under docs/ ships only when someone adds it here on
# purpose. Every `!` below carries the reason it exists.

# Private office source files — the app ships no spreadsheet.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm
*.csv
*.numbers
*.ods
# Arabic belongs in the translation CSV, and only there, so it is the one .csv
# that ships.
!apex/translations/
!apex/translations/*.csv

# Internal notes and design documents are markdown, and docs/ is internal by
# default; the published set is named one file at a time below.
*.md
docs/*
# Deliberately NOT anchored to the repo root: matching README.md at every depth is
# what keeps apex/change_log/README.md (the in-app changelog index) and the
# frontend package READMEs shipping. Rewriting this as `!/README.md` drops them.
!README.md
# The portal design guide ships with the workspace it governs: a builder working from a
# clone has to be able to read the tokens, the scales and the archetypes.
!frontend/frontend_shared/DESIGN.md
# Frappe's "Updated To A New Version" popup reads these as shipped app files.
!apex/change_log/v*/*.md
# The three flat pages these lines used to publish were replaced by the per-audience
# structure below; naming a file that no longer exists publishes nothing and hides that the
# real allowlist is the two directory globs.
# Public per-area training guide: index plus one file per functional area.
!docs/training/
!docs/training/*.md
# The refresher lessons and the per-role tracks the index links. Both were tracked
# already but matched no `!` line, so a new page in either sub-directory could reach the
# repository only by force-add — the allowlist has to name the depth it publishes.
!docs/training/lessons/
!docs/training/lessons/*.md
!docs/training/tracks/
!docs/training/tracks/*.md
# Operator runbooks; the pre-rename app-identity cutover path lives here.
!docs/administration/
!docs/administration/*.md
# Canonical inventories the other pages link instead of copying. Two of them are
# generated from the shipped JSON, so a hand edit here is overwritten, not merged.
!docs/reference/
!docs/reference/*.md
# Screenshots a lesson links, one directory per lesson, captured from synthetic rows.
# Every parent has to be un-ignored first: git never descends into an ignored directory,
# so a rule naming only the file matches nothing and the image can reach the repository
# only by force-add.
!docs/assets/
!docs/assets/training/
!docs/assets/training/*/
!docs/assets/training/*/*.png
